-- =============================================================================
-- NOTES / THINGS TO CHECK BEFORE PUBLISHING THE NUMBERS
--
-- 1. PLATFORM FILTER IS OFF until you fill `us_platforms` from Q0. As written this is all-Visa.
--
-- 2. Amount scale. wdp.action carries both a_dispute_amt and i_dispute_currency_exponent.
--    This query sums a_dispute_amt as stored (numeric(20,4)). If the exponent is ever non-2 the
--    values need scaling - confirm with:
--      SELECT i_dispute_currency_exponent, COUNT(*) FROM wdp.action
--      WHERE c_case_stage='CH1' AND c_action_type='FCHG' GROUP BY 1;
--    a_cnverted_dispute_amt / a_dispute_workable_amt are the alternatives if you want the
--    converted or workable figure instead of the as-reported one.
--
-- 3. Multi-currency. Only sum across currencies once distinct_currencies = 1, or add
--    c_dispute_currency to the GROUP BY.
--
-- 4. Date column. d_action_reported is when the network reported the chargeback. Use
--    d_action_processed if the report is meant to track when WDP handled it, and note that
--    z_insrt is not reliably UTC (see D-ACTION-PROCESSED-EST-FEASIBILITY.md).
--
-- 5. Cost. Both queries scan wdp.action; ix_action_reported_date / ix_action_brin_reported_date
--    cover the d_action_reported predicate, which is why the window is applied there.
--
-- 6. Out-of-scope codes (10.1, 10.2, 10.3, 13.8, 13.9) and accept-recommend (10.5) fall out of
--    cases_eligible automatically by not being in target_codes; they still appear in the gross
--    rows, which is the point of the gross/eligible split.
